Here is a complete, self-contained HTML5 Snake game. You can save this code as an `.html` file (e.g., `snake.html`) and open it in any modern web browser.

### Features:
- **Classic Gameplay**: Eat food to grow, avoid walls and yourself.
- **Controls**: Arrow keys or WASD.
- **Score Tracking**: Current score and high score (stored in `localStorage`).
- **Game States**: Start screen, playing, and game over screens.
- **Responsive**: Works on desktop and mobile (touch controls included).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>HTML5 Snake Game</title>
    <style>
        body {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #2c3e50;
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            color: #ecf0f1;
        }

        h1 {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            color: #2ecc71;
        }

        .game-container {
            position: relative;
            box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
            border-radius: 8px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        canvas {
            display: block;
            background-color: #34495e;
        }

        .score-board {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            width: 400px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            font-size: 1.2em;
        }

        .overlay {
            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        .overlay.hidden {
            display: none;
        }

        .btn {
            background-color: #2ecc71;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            cursor: pointer;
            border-radius: 5px;
            margin-top: 15px;
            transition: background-color 0.3s;
        }

        .btn:hover {
            background-color: #27ae60;
        }

        .instructions {
            font-size: 0.9em;
            color: #bdc3c7;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Snake Game</h1>
    
    <div class="score-board">
        <span>Score: <span id="score">0</span></span>
        <span>High Score: <span id="highScore">0</span></span>
    </div>

    <div class="game-container">
        <canvas id="gameCanvas" width="400" height="400"></canvas>
        
        <!-- Start Screen -->
        <div id="startScreen" class="overlay">
            <h2>Ready to Play?</h2>
            <p>Use Arrow Keys or WASD to move.</p>
            <button class="btn" onclick="startGame()">Start Game</button>
        </div>

        <!-- Game Over Screen -->
        <div id="gameOverScreen" class="overlay hidden">
            <h2>Game Over!</h2>
            <p>Your Score: <span id="finalScore">0</span></p>
            <button class="btn" onclick="startGame()">Play Again</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="instructions">
        <p>Controls: Arrow Keys or WASD</p>
    </div>


